# SRG-APP-000098-AU-000710  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must produce audit records containing information
# to establish the source of the events.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000098-AU-000710
group:           V-221911
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000133
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    For records that arrive without a host already set, Splunk derives the
                 origin from the sending system: connection_host = ip uses the sender's
                 address and dns uses its reverse DNS name.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.

check:           inputs.conf [] connection_host not_equals none

external:        Reverse DNS correctness where connection_host = dns rests on the DNS
                 service; the specification requires the forward lookup to match the
                 reverse lookup.
external:        Hosts forwarding over the Splunk-to-Splunk protocol set the host on the
                 sending side, and connection_host applies only where the sender leaves it
                 unset.

citation:        Unmatchable condition corrected. The original stanza [<network input
                 stanza>] is prose, not a stanza name, and assess.sh compares stanza names
                 literally, so the condition never matched and the row returned absent on
                 every instance. The determined row carries no stanza, and connection_host
                 occurs only in network input stanzas (tcp, udp, splunktcp and their token
                 variants, and [http://name] for HEC), so the key scopes the condition
                 without a stanza. Qualifier for the assessor: inputs.conf.spec says "none"
                 leaves the host "as specified in inputs.conf", so where none is paired
                 with an explicit per-input host the origin is still established; read
                 inputs.conf host before citing this, as ANDed conditions cannot express
                 that pairing.
finding:         A network input is configured with connection_host = none and no explicit
                 host, so records arriving on it are stamped with the log server's own
                 hostname and the source of the event cannot be established.
